Ok. Here are some things which you will have to do to get the game up and 
running.  

1.  First put all files except Space-Boot in a subdirectory under JMP: called
    SEdata.  This is where all the files will be saved.  Also during game
    play the game will create some file which I put in a arexx program called
    GameNews.rexx.   This is on the logon scence which ask the users if they
    wish to read SE news files.   At this time you have three files you can
    show them.  First one, is called  ydaynews.txt, which this file tells
    what happened in SE the day before.  Second news.txt, which tells what has
    happened on SE today. Finally, a file called scores.txt and scores.txt.ans
    these two files will list out the stats of all the people.  You will see
    there score, name and total planets.
    
2.  Go into the SPCEMP.CFG file and change what ever you want in there.  There
    is a line at the bottom with a short description of what the line does.

3.   This is the big one.  It isn't required but if you don't do it the
     option is justleft out.  There isn't no way around it.  You have to
     create a Message base if you want players to leave message between each
     other.  Call it Space Empire.  After this you have to setup of the 
     message base text file that goes with a Message Base.  There is an
     example one with the Arc file.  Take a look at it and rearrange the text
     file to your settings.  You will notice that the @MC line is at the
     bottom of the text file.  You have to leave it there if you want the
     text file to work.  Make Sure you leave the Name to 'Space' ,     
     'Space.ans' and 'Space.sky'.   Otherwise the program will not find it
     and the users will not be able to leave messages in there.  There is a
     program out there that lets you leave message using an different name.
     That would be the best since the game lets you uses alias's in the game.
     I put the alias in there because I hate having to use my name in a game.
     Some times people will pick on you because they know who you are, but
     picking another name lets that user be free from that sort of thing until
     they find out who he is.


